<title>USA: TABLE - ESCELSA sells $500 mln 10-yr 144a notes.</title>
<headline>TABLE - ESCELSA sells $500 mln 10-yr 144a notes.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following 144a debt issue from Espirito Santo Centrais Eletricas S.A. (ESCELSA) was priced on Wednesday via Morgan Stanley, Dean Witter, Discover &amp; Co, according to a market source.</p>
<p>ESCELSA, which was the first electric utility privatized under Brazil's electric industry reform, distributes electricity in the State of Espirito Santo in Brazil</p>
<p>The deal was increased to $500 million from an amount of $350 million.</p>
<p>BORROWER ESCELSA</p>
<p>AMT $500 MLN	   COUPON 10.00 PCT  MATURITY 7/15/2007</p>
<p>TYPE SNR UNSEC NOTES ISS PRICE 99.875  FIRST PAY DATE 1/1/1998</p>
<p>LAST MOODY'S B1	YIELD 10.019 PCT  PAY FREQ  SEMI-ANNUAL</p>
<p>LAST S&amp;P BB-MINUS    SPREAD 387.5 BPS  CALLABLE  NO</p>
<p>((U.S. Corporate Bond Unit, 212-859-1678))</p>
